.\n                    ', 'gen_ai.response.id': 'chatcmpl-222bfd1051b74022b1a98bb245dc87be', 'gen_ai.response.model': 'models/Qwen2.5-3B-Instruct', 'gen_ai.usage.total_tokens': 1203, 'gen_ai.usage.prompt_tokens': 1046, 'gen_ai.usage.completion_tokens': 157, 'gen_ai.completion.0.finish_reason': 'stop', 'gen_ai.completion.0.role': 'assistant', 'gen_ai.completion.0.content': "1. **Justification:**  \nThe query asks to find \\( p(t) \\) using Abel's theorem given that the Wronskian of two solutions of a second-order linear differential equation is a non-zero constant. The Generalist_Solution_Generator_Tool can be used to derive this result, as it is capable of performing mathematical derivations and manipulations.\n\n2. **Context:**  \nNo additional context is needed beyond the user's query and previous steps.\n\n3. **Sub-Goal:**  \nDerive \\( p(t) \\) using Abel's theorem, given that the Wronskian \\( W(t_0) = k \\), where \\( k \\) is a non-zero constant.\n\n4. **Tool Name:** Generalist_Solution_Generator_Tool", 'prompt_token_ids': [151644, 8948, 198, 2610, 525, 264, 10950, 11, 11521, 11, 323, 7785, 17847, 13, 151645, 198, 151644, 872, 271, 6262, 25, 29901, 279, 22823, 1790, 3019, 311, 2621, 279, 3239, 1667, 2500, 7375, 323, 3681, 7354, 382, 1972, 510, 12, 3070, 2859, 66963, 16246, 279, 2086, 23810, 13482, 40164, 23606, 17767, 1124, 37018, 90, 67, 61, 17, 87, 15170, 8047, 61, 17, 92, 488, 281, 1155, 10699, 37018, 90, 12719, 15170, 8047, 92, 488, 2804, 1155, 50724, 284, 220, 15, 1124, 701, 1477, 279, 729, 17767, 281, 1155, 8, 1124, 8, 421, 279, 467, 2248, 4886, 1103, 315, 1378, 9904, 17767, 856, 62, 16, 1155, 8, 1124, 8, 323, 17767, 856, 62, 17, 1155, 8, 1124, 8, 374, 264, 2477, 36929, 6783, 13, 5443, 86849, 594, 57817, 311, 8253, 17767, 281, 1155, 8, 1124, 568, 3197, 5527, 11, 2550, 279, 1590, 4226, 43810, 304, 366, 9217, 29, 323, 690, 9217, 29, 9492, 13, 3155, 537, 6923, 894, 2213, 1283, 279, 690, 9217, 29, 4772, 624, 12, 3070, 2859, 18320, 66963, 3070, 19237, 315, 2